From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sechost: SERVICE_CONFIG_PREFERRED_NODE, TraceSetInformation, TraceQueryInformation (3673)

sechost: SERVICE_CONFIG_PREFERRED_NODE, TraceSetInformation, TraceQueryInformation

QueryServiceConfig2/ChangeServiceConfig2 (A and W) now handle level 9: the
preferred NUMA node is kept in the service key (PreferredNode), fDelete removes
it, a node above the highest node is ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER.
TraceSetInformation validates every class as documented (ERROR_BAD_LENGTH,
ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER, ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED); provider binary tracking and
compression are kept per session and read back by TraceQueryInformation, which
moves from advapi32 to sechost (where Windows exports it). The kernel capture
classes are accepted on the kernel logger only.

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 3214 (fast-a): SERVICE_CONFIG_PREFERRED_NODE was implemented twice; 3214's (services.exe rpc.c, svcctl.idl prefnode member, sechost conversion) kept, 3673's duplicate rpc.c cases and idl lines dropped (its sechost/service.c hunks were already identical). 3673 keeps TraceSetInformation/TraceQueryInformation.
